except components expressly licensed separately. Licensors are the respective
copyright holders granting rights they own. Existing separately released versions
keep their terms; no third-party rights are granted without authority.

1. Free community grant. Subject to these conditions, individuals may use the
software personally, and one organization may use it internally with up to 20
enabled human accounts, including for its own commercial activities. Copying,
building, deploying and modifying for those purposes is permitted. Retain Shennian
interface branding, logos and copyright displays, and applicable source and
artifact license and attribution notices. Count enabled human accounts using
Shennian, not all employees. Exclude agents, bots and disabled accounts;
deduplicate devices and aggregate deployments of the same organization.
Splitting instances does not increase the allowance.

2. Applications and outputs. This license claims no rights to your independently
created applications, content or business data. You may use the software's explicit
permission mechanisms to share your own developed or registered local applications
and their business entry points. Visitors without an enabled Shennian account do
not count as registered accounts merely by accessing those applications. This is
not a grant to host, resell or white-label the Shennian platform itself. You remain
responsible for your applications, shared data and visitor notices.

3. Additional authorization. Prior written authorization is required if you exceed
20 enabled human accounts OR remove, replace or hide Shennian interface branding,
logos or copyright displays. Commercial hosting of Shennian for third parties,
multi-customer services, white-label distribution and resale require separate
authorization. Organization, user scope, term and permitted interface changes are
agreed in writing. No fixed public price is stated. Contact the Shennian team via
WeCom at https://shennian.net/#contact.

4. Redistribution. Within the permitted scope, include this license with source,
modified versions and built artifacts, retain applicable notices, identify changes,
and do not imply official endorsement. Recipients receive the corresponding rights
licensors can grant under these terms; broader use requires authorization.
Third-party components and separately licensed files retain their own licenses.
Shennian white-label permission does not waive third-party license or attribution
obligations, including NOTICE, fonts and assets.

5. No technical lock or service commitment. No activation key, online license
verification or member-data reporting is required. Expiry does not automatically
lock machines or delete data; absence of a lock does not authorize broader use.
Renew commercial authorization or return to the free scope when it expires. This
license does not include deployment, migration, training, customization, technical
support, response-time commitments or continuing-update promises.

6. Reserved rights and liability. Rights not expressly granted are reserved.
Unlicensed use outside these terms is not authorized; stopping it does not waive
existing liability. Software is provided AS IS, without warranties to the extent
permitted by applicable law. Copyright holders exclude liability only as permitted
by law; mandatory liability is not excluded.

